<title>USA: Norfolk Southern sees 15 pct EPS growth.</title>
<headline>Norfolk Southern sees 15 pct EPS growth.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norfolk Southern Corp said Tuesday it expects that by the year 2000 quarterly earnings per share would increase by 15 percent over the first quarter of 1998, when the company hopes its acquisition of part of Conrail Inc would be complete.</p>
<p>Norfolk Chief Executive David Goode, in remarks to the annual International Intermodal Expo in Atlanta, said the prediction is &quot;calculated on the challenging base of our EPS plan with aggressive share repurchase.&quot;</p>
<p>He said the company would get a 50 percent revenue increase immediately upon merging.</p>
</text>
